From afd98666c4345f2914fb836e00534a8c9746e6f0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:25:19 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] dma-direct: check CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_DMA_SET_UNCACHED before
 set_uncached

set_uncached is a local that can only be true when
CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_DMA_SET_UNCACHED is enabled.  Make that explicit in the
condition so that a compiler which does not propagate the constant
through the variable still drops the arch_dma_set_uncached() call.
No functional change.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 kernel/dma/direct.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/kernel/dma/direct.c b/kernel/dma/direct.c
index da665ca22..1615e9dc4 100644
--- a/kernel/dma/direct.c
+++ b/kernel/dma/direct.c
@@ -326,7 +326,7 @@ void *dma_direct_alloc(struct device *dev, size_t size,
 
 	memset(cpu_addr, 0, size);
 
-	if (set_uncached) {
+	if (IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_ARCH_HAS_DMA_SET_UNCACHED) && set_uncached) {
 		void *uncached_cpu_addr;
 
 		arch_dma_prep_coherent(page, size);
